All 258 tests pass. 

The change is complete. The `POST /api/owners` endpoint now rejects creation with **409 Conflict** when another owner already has the same last name and telephone number.

**What I changed** — `ClinicServiceImpl.isSameIdentity` (the predicate behind `existsIdenticalOwner`, already wired into `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`):

```java
private boolean isSameIdentity(Owner existing, Owner candidate) {
    return Objects.equals(existing.getLastName(), candidate.getLastName())
        && Objects.equals(existing.getTelephone(), candidate.getTelephone());
}
```

It previously required *all five* fields (first name, last name, address, city, telephone) to match. Now the conflict rule triggers on last name + telephone alone, per the spec. The controller already returns `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` when this returns true, and the existing `existsIdenticalOwner` query narrows candidates by last name, so the check stays efficient.

The pre-existing `Cp02Tests` (the checkpoint for this rule) and all other tests — including the V1 controller's duplicate-conflict test and the "same last name, different telephone is allowed" case — pass.

